# FILLET Benchmark 1 with HEXTOR 4.2.1-42-g75f5fb1
# Model: HEXTOR 4.2.1-42-g75f5fb1 (FILLET re-file, September 2026); 18 latitude belts of 10 deg, seasonal cycle, explicit 730 steps per orbit (dt = 43226.5 s, set by nstepyr).
# Radiation: 1 bar lookup table ./radiation/radiation_N2_CO2_Sun.h5 (clear sky; CO2 axis 100 ppm - 0.91, T 190-370 K with power-law extrapolation outside; CO2 below 100 ppm is clamped to the axis floor); no cloud albedo (fcloud = 0); cloudir = 9.37 W m^-2 (tuned so that Benchmark 1 reaches 288 K).
# Transport: d0 = 0.38 rescaled at run time by pressure, composition and rotation (diffadj; 1.101 for 1 bar N2 at 280 ppm), the published Earth transport; the Diff column is the value used.
# Surface: Fresnel ocean albedo, land 0.30, snow/ice 0.663; heat capacities land 5.25e6, water 2.1e8, ice 1.05e7 J m^-2 K^-1; present-day geography, ocean fraction 0.7; sea-ice fraction 1 - exp((T - 273.15 K)/10 K) between 273.15 and 263.15 K and 1 below; land snow below 273.15 K.
# Orbit: a = 1 au, e = 0, year 365.22 d.
# Initial state: uniform 288 K (warm start) or 233 K (cold start) as noted per experiment; every case starts from that state (no continuation).
# Convergence: halt when the year-to-year change in global-mean OLR falls below 1e-03 W m^-2, or when it repeats to that tolerance over a cycle of up to 4 years (a periodic seasonal oscillation; the case then reports one phase of the cycle) (cap 5000 orbits); one further orbit provides the annual means. Per-case records in logs/.
# Numerics switches: diffcons = .true..
#
# Name of benchmark/experiment: Benchmark 1
# Case number: 0
# Instellation (S_earth): 1.0000
# XCO2 (ppm): 280.0000
# Obliquity (degrees): 23.5
# Initial state: uniform 288 K
# Convergence: 25 orbits, year-to-year OLR test met; final year-to-year |dOLR| = 8.087e-04 W m^-2, |dTglob| = 3.498e-04 K; north-south asymmetry of the annual-mean belt temperatures = 5.0816 K
#
# Columns of data (annually averaged for last orbit)
# Lat = latitude of belt centre (degrees)
# Tsurf = annual mean surface temperature (K)
# Asurf = insolation-weighted annual mean surface albedo
# ATOA = insolation-weighted annual mean top-of-atmosphere/planetary albedo (1 - ASR/S)
# OLR = annual mean outgoing longwave radiation (W m^-2)
# Lat Tsurf Asurf ATOA OLR
